Build a smart grocery price comparison web app (single HTML file) with the following features:
Core functionality:

Search bar with autocomplete suggestions for common Indian grocery items (bread, milk, eggs, fruits, diapers, FMCG etc.)
Add multiple items to a basket with − / qty / + stepper controls (clearly visible quantity per item)
On compare, use the Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514) to fetch realistic 2025 Indian market prices for each item across Blinkit, Swiggy Instamart, and Zepto

Pricing display:

Always show the actual selling price (after discount), NOT the MRP
Show MRP crossed out alongside the selling price
Show discount % badge (e.g. "49% off") per item per platform
Example: Mamy Poko XL 52pcs → MRP ₹1352, selling price ₹686
FMCG/baby/personal care: 30–55% off MRP. Fresh produce/dairy: 5–15% off MRP

Comparison views:

Platform total cards (Blinkit / Swiggy / Zepto) showing total cost, MRP, discount %, and "Best deal" badge
Item breakdown table with per-unit price, selling total, MRP, discount % — green = cheapest, grey = most expensive
Split platform strategy: suggest buying each item from whichever platform is cheapest, show combined total and savings vs. single app

Card offers (user has Amazon Pay, IDFC First, HDFC cards):

HDFC Swiggy CC: 10% cashback on Swiggy Instamart (cap ₹1500/month), 5% on Blinkit (cap ₹250)
IDFC FIRST SWYP: 10% instant off on Zepto (cap ₹100, min ₹750); ₹100 flat off Zepto on Fridays (min ₹999)
Amazon Pay: 5% cashback for Prime members when paying via Amazon Pay on Blinkit
Show applicable offers based on the user's basket total per platform, calculate actual rupee savings, show "after card offer" final price

Coupon unlock tip:

AI should suggest adding one cheap product to hit a round threshold (₹750 or ₹999) to unlock a bigger card discount
Example: "Add Colgate 200g (₹89) to Zepto to hit ₹999 and unlock IDFC ₹100 off"

Final savings summary:

Show: MRP total → after platform discounts → after best card offer → total rupees saved

Design: Dark theme, DM Sans font, mobile-friendly, clean card-based layout with color-coded platform dots (Blinkit yellow, Swiggy orange, Zepto purple)
Tech: Single index.html file, vanilla JS, Claude API via fetch() for price estimation, no backend needed
